	(text "POWER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "28101d35-e0bb-51f0-bf28-db035ee48626")
	)
	(text "Console +5V (edge land 25, CONS_5V) and USB VBUS are diode-ORed into +5V: neither source can\nback-feed the other (an unpowered console, or the USB host).  SS34 VF ~0.35 V at the cart's ~0.4 A,\nso +5V is 4.4-4.9 V; there is no 5 V logic on this board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3331174-3dee-50aa-aa07-f7bdf4e84b21")
	)
	(text "AP63203 3.3 V / 2 A buck: ESP32-S3 (WiFi bursts ~400 mA), CP2102N, microSD.  4 ms soft-start (tSS)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "32ab1cc9-3b77-574e-8598-347654913efd")
	)
	(text "AP2112K-3.3 LDO -> +3V3_RP: the WHOLE RP2354A (IOVDD, QSPI/USB/ADC supplies, VREG_VIN + VREG_AVDD).\nIn dropout it follows +5V as the console rail rises (1 V/ms into 21 uF = 21 mA, under the 50 mA\nfold-back limit), so the 5 V-tolerant pads are never unpowered with the console bus driving them\n(RP2350 datasheet: FT pads tolerate 5.5 V \"provided IOVDD is powered to 3.3 V\").\nThe buck instead waits for UVLO, then soft-starts over 4 ms.  VREG_VIN and VREG_AVDD rise together (p.402)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e1c61867-e932-5f7d-be47-78e4ca4e9fc7")
	)
	(text "PWR_FLAGs: the rails above are driven through diodes / inductors (passive pins)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2211803a-3ca6-5966-bb2a-2a8c236e7ffa")
	)
